# --- Help & troubleshooting section (Dashboard) ---
DMMHelpAndTroubleshooting = Help & troubleshooting
DMMSeeHelpSection = See the Help & troubleshooting section at the bottom of the Dashboard.
DMMHelpQuickStartTitle = Quick start
DMMHelpQuickStartBody = 1) Add a GitHub token or a public repository in the Sources tab. 2) Click "Refresh all sources" on the Dashboard to discover modules. 3) Open a module and click Install or Update. Backups are taken automatically before every update.
DMMHelpConceptsTitle = Key concepts
DMMHelpConceptSources = Sources|Where DMM finds modules: a GitHub token (your private repos), a hub (a dmmhub.json list of repos), the Dolibarr community index, or the DoliStore catalog. Each registered module shows a badge for its source.
DMMHelpConceptChannels = Stable vs Dev channel|Stable tracks published releases (tags). Dev follows the HEAD of a development branch (latest commit) and is only available when Developer mode is on.
DMMHelpConceptTokens = Token auto-matching|When you add a token, DMM matches it to the private repositories it can read. A module showing "Needs token" just means no current token can read it yet — add the right token and refresh, the badge clears itself.
DMMHelpConceptBackups = Backups & retention|Every update copies the current module aside first. Restore rolls it back atomically (the module is never left missing, even if a restore fails). Old backups are pruned by age (days) and by count per module, both set in Advanced.
DMMHelpConceptGitlab = Self-hosted GitLab|Besides GitHub, DMM installs from self-hosted GitLab instances (e.g. git.open-dsi.fr, framagit.org), including modules living in a subdirectory of a monorepo. Add the repo URL in Sources.
DMMHelpTroubleTitle = Troubleshooting
DMMHelpTroublePerms = "Failed to stage/copy" on install or restore|The web user cannot write inside custom/. The error message names the exact user and the chown/chmod command to run. Your module is never damaged when this happens — it stays as it was.
DMMHelpTroubleNeedToken = A module is stuck on "Needs token"|Its repository is private and none of your tokens can read it. Add a token with access in Sources, then click "Refresh all sources".
DMMHelpTroubleRateLimit = GitHub rate limit reached|Unauthenticated GitHub calls are capped at 60/hour. Add a token (even for public repos, enable "Use for public") to raise the limit to 5000/hour.
DMMHelpRunPreflight = Run preflight diagnostics (PHP, permissions, GitHub connectivity)
DMMChannelTooltip = Stable installs published releases (tags). Dev follows the latest commit on a development branch. Only registered git-backed modules can use Dev, and only when Developer mode is on.
DMMSourceColumnTooltip = How DMM knows about this module: Token = one of your GitHub tokens' repos; Hub = imported from a dmmhub.json list; Community = the official Dolibarr community index; DoliStore = the DoliStore catalog.
DMMNoReposVisible = This token exposes no repositories, so no modules could be discovered. Check that the token is valid and not expired, that it has the 'repo' / 'Contents' read permission, and — for a fine-grained token — that the repositories you want are selected in the token's settings on GitHub.
